Package: lenovo-yoga-c940-14iil-support
Architecture: all
Depends: convertible-helper (>= 1.3.0), convertible-power (>= 1.0.0), grub-large-console (>= 1.0.0),
         firmware-iwlwifi, firmware-intel-misc, firmware-intel-graphics, firmware-sof-signed,
         alsa-ucm-conf, alsa-topology-conf, iio-sensor-proxy, bluez, udev, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: thermald, bolt, v4l-utils, fprintd, libpam-fprintd, intel-media-va-driver
Description: Lenovo Yoga C940-14IIL (81Q9) hardware support for Debian
 Settings and firmware dependencies for the Lenovo Yoga C940-14IIL (type 81Q9,
 Ice Lake Core i7) on a stock Debian GNOME desktop: Wi-Fi and Bluetooth
 firmware (AX201), Smart Sound (SOF) audio firmware and UCM profiles, Intel
 graphics firmware, auto-rotate (iio-sensor-proxy), tablet mode
 (convertible-helper), power management (convertible-power plus this laptop's
 TLP settings) and readable GRUB text (grub-large-console).
 .
 The fingerprint reader (06cb:00be) has no free driver and cannot be made to
 work from the Debian archive; fprintd is only recommended.  See README.md.
 .
 The settings are applied only when the DMI product version is
 "Lenovo Yoga C940-14IIL".
